.TH TARGET 10 "October 2026" "1.1" "Neverdark Manual"
.SH NAME
target \- Set or show your default target region
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B target
.br
.B target
.I region
.br
.B target here
.br
.B target none
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Commands that act on a region \fBwall\fP, \fBban\fP, \fBunban\fP,
\fBloadmod\fP, \fBunloadmod\fP, \fBmodlist\fP and \fBdeny\fP \fBnormally take an
optional region selector. Without one they act on your \fBdefault target
region\fP if you have set one, and otherwise on the region you are standing in.
.PP
This command shows or changes that default.
.TP
.B target
Show the current default, or say that there is none.
.TP
.BI target " region"
Set the default. \fIregion\fP is a bare world number (0\-65535) or the keyword
\fBcosmos\fP, under exactly the same rules every other region selector uses.
You must rule the region you name, or an ancestor of it, or the command is
refused and names the ruler.
.TP
.B target here
Set the default to the region you are standing in, without having to name it.
That is the deepest region the engine knows about there \-\- a claimed world, or
the cosmos from the void \-\- not a single cell: only worlds are claimed, and a
cell selector would reach nobody. From the void this stores the cosmos, which no
world number can name.
.TP
.B target none
Clear the default. Commands go back to acting on your current region.
.PP
The default is validated \fBwhen you set it\fP, not when a command uses it, so
it cannot be a setting that appears to work and then refuses every command.
.PP
Note the asymmetry: \fBloadmod\fP and \fBunloadmod\fP require \fBexact\fP
ownership of the named region, because module loading attaches to one specific
region row. A default naming a subregion you rule but do not own outright is
therefore settable here and refused by those two commands. That is correct
rather than a defect.
.PP
The default applies only to commands that take a region selector. It does not
change what \fBowned\fP, \fBclone\fP, \fBcreate\fP or \fBchown\fP may reach:
those are scoped to the region of the \fIobject\fP involved, so setting a default
is never a way to widen what you can enumerate or act on by name.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wall,ban,unban,modlist,loadmod,unloadmod,deny,here,planet (10)
.SH AUTHOR
quirinpa <quirinpa@tty.pt>
